    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49733" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ūnănĭmus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		unus-animus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of one mind</i>, <i>heart</i>, or <i>will; of one accord</i>, <i>concordant</i>, <i>harmonious</i>, <i>unanimous</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ego tu sum, tu's ego: unanimi sumus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Stich. 5, 4, 49</span></i>
			 ritschl <i>N. cr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sodales,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					30, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fratres,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 8, 669</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 1, 615</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 161</span></i> (but
			in <i><span class="en">Liv.
				7, 21, 5</span></i>, the correct read. is una animos).</div>
